lemma exists_of_equivalent_index {ι κ : Type*} (e : ι ≃ κ) (P : ι → Prop)
    (i : ι) (hi : P i) : ∃ b : κ, P (e.symm b) := by
  exact ⟨e i, (e.symm_apply_apply i).symm ▸ hi⟩

/- Main reduction. Write `q = 2^j * q'` with `q'` odd and `r - j = u + 1`. A group `G` of order
`2^k * q` is an extension, with kernel the normal core of a Sylow 2-subgroup, of a group of order
`2^c * q'` (`c ≤ q'!`) by a group of order `2^(k+j-c)`. The quotient is generated by `c + u`
elements, so lifting them gives a template: the class of the kernel, the class of the quotient,
and the `c + u` images in the automorphism group of the kernel. The number of templates is at
most `(q'! + 1) * A * M`, where `A` bounds the classes of quotients and `M` is a moment of
automorphism groups of 2-groups, bounded by the global moment hypothesis. Every weight is at most `2^((k+j)(2^L q')²)`,
and the endpoint estimate bounds `g (2^(k+r))` from below; the comparison is `poly_ineq`. -/
set_option maxHeartbeats 700000 in
